I've written the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file are in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored; the plan's own commit command ends in || true, which suggests that was expected. The files are on disk for the implementation phase.

**task_01 — Part of #1016 (product):** what happens to held piped `-p` text if the event loop panics. This is the last exit on #1016's list still open. Step 1 is a probe: drop the held-text buffer during a panic and record the exact bytes that reach the output. I expect them to be empty (text lost), but haven't measured it yet. If they're not empty, the task stops there with "probed: nothing lost on panic". If they are, step 2 flushes the held text when the buffer is dropped, but only while the program is panicking. On every normal drop, behaviour stays exactly as it is today, so a discarded retry attempt can never leak into the output. It includes tests for the normal-drop and retry cases, plus a break-and-restore check. The commit will state its limits: builds set to abort on panic aren't covered, and the task must check whether the panic actually reaches the buffer through tokio.

**task_02 — Part of #869 (product), the backlog-drain slot:** the oldest open issue, #858, needs a human to edit a protected file, so this slot goes to the next oldest, #869. auto_context_for_prompt runs on every REPL turn and can attach files to the model's prompt from a directory that a /cd config denies. The task:
• states up front where the new check goes: beside the existing check, as the earlier #869 slices did;
• requires the shortcut taken when there are no startup restrictions to check the /cd list too, so a half-fix can't pass the register guard;
• shrinks `UNWIRED_CHECK_PATH_READERS` by exactly one;
• updates the size-gate entry for commands_project.rs, which is already 8 lines past its recorded 3645.

